// Molly's provenance unit test "repeat rule firings with different contributing tuples (missing fields are
// wildcards)" (R06 §12.6, ProvenanceSuite): c(loc, 1) has two distinct derivations, through proxy(loc, x, 1) and
// proxy(loc, y, 1), although the rule mentions the middle column only as `_`. Blossom golden corpus, transcribed from
// R06 (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

proxy("loc", A, B) :- a(L, A, B);
c(L, V) :- b(L, V), proxy(L, _, V);

a("loc", "x", 1)@1;
a("loc", "y", 1)@1;
b("loc", 1)@1;
